==> omaddons install -h <==
Install or update addons in one target, verified by its own TOC rules

Usage: omaddons install [OPTIONS] <REF>...
Aliases: add

Arguments:
  <REF>...  What to install: a catalog name (weakauras), owner/repo, a canonical ref (gh:, git:,
            url:, file:, wowi:, tukui:), a pasted GitHub or https link, or a path to a zip or folder

Options:
      --channel <CHANNEL>  stable, beta or alpha (default: the addon's recorded channel, then
                           default_channel, then stable)
      --version <VERSION>  Install exactly this release: a tag for gh: refs, a rev for git: refs
      --file <ZIP>         Install this downloaded archive as the release of the one given ref
      --reinstall          Install the recorded release again, replacing its folders (repairs
                           modified or missing files)
      --no-deps            Install only the named addons, not the ones their TOCs require
      --force              Take over a folder another addon owns, an addon of the same name from
                           another ref, or replace an unmanaged folder
      --strict             Exit 6 when only some of the addons install
      --refresh            Fetch every release from its source, never from remembered metadata
      --any-flavor         On this client, install builds the publisher did not make for it (kept by
                           every later update and sync until --no-any-flavor)
      --no-any-flavor      Clear --any-flavor for these addons on this client

Examples:
  omaddons install dbm bigwigs -t retail  catalog names, in one transaction
  omaddons install gh:tullamods/OmniCC --dry-run
                                          preview it, and store the plan
  omaddons install ./MyAddon.zip -t era   a local zip or folder

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons install --help <==
Install or update addons in one target, verified by its own TOC rules

Usage: omaddons install [OPTIONS] <REF>...
Aliases: add

Arguments:
  <REF>...
          What to install: a catalog name (weakauras), owner/repo, a canonical ref (gh:, git:, url:,
          file:, wowi:, tukui:), a pasted GitHub or https link, or a path to a zip or folder

Options:
      --channel <CHANNEL>
          stable, beta or alpha (default: the addon's recorded channel, then default_channel, then
          stable)

      --version <VERSION>
          Install exactly this release: a tag for gh: refs, a rev for git: refs

      --file <ZIP>
          Install this downloaded archive as the release of the one given ref

      --reinstall
          Install the recorded release again, replacing its folders (repairs modified or missing
          files)

      --no-deps
          Install only the named addons, not the ones their TOCs require

      --force
          Take over a folder another addon owns, an addon of the same name from another ref, or
          replace an unmanaged folder

      --strict
          Exit 6 when only some of the addons install

      --refresh
          Fetch every release from its source, never from remembered metadata

      --any-flavor
          On this client, install builds the publisher did not make for it (kept by every later
          update and sync until --no-any-flavor)

      --no-any-flavor
          Clear --any-flavor for these addons on this client

Examples:
  omaddons install dbm bigwigs -t retail  catalog names, in one transaction
  omaddons install gh:tullamods/OmniCC --dry-run
                                          preview it, and store the plan
  omaddons install ./MyAddon.zip -t era   a local zip or folder

An addon is installed from one ref at a time. Another local archive of a local
install (./Bar-2.2.0.zip over ./Bar-2.1.0.zip) updates it; an addon of the same
name from any other ref is a takeover, refused (ownership_conflict) unless --force.

See also: search, apply, undo

Global options:
      --json              One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>   Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>   The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the
                          Classic Era client), family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every
                          client) [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run           Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change
                          nothing)
      --actor <ACTOR>     Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>     Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by
                          commands that change nothing)
      --offline           Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running     Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --if-match <TOKEN>  Change nothing unless the plan is still the one the --dry-run that
                          returned this token (data.precondition) showed
      --no-color          No ANSI color
      --no-progress       No progress output
      --progress <MODE>   Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet             Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...        More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help              Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
